    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1609">

                <pb facs="1014" n="898" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.93/61.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Vice Consul Simpich.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 24, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Exert every possible influence to prevent hostile action against Chinese or any
                    other foreigners. Ask Carranza to furnish necessary force to restrain mob. Give
                    asylum to any foreigners whose lives are in danger. If necessary conduct them to
                    American side and hold them and care for them until you receive further
                    instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
